# Roboter Studio named-object grasping: return the fixed object catalog as
# parallel per-type arrays. type_names[i] is the internal type key (the Blockly
# block field value); labels_de[i] is its German display label. The render
# arrays (object_height_m, object_width_m, color_hex) let the simulation editor
# draw each object at its real catalog size and colour instead of a fixed box;
# max_instances[i] = len(tag_ids) is how many copies of that type the sim can
# detect, so the 2D editor caps placement at it. Every array is parallel — same
# length, same catalog order. The catalog is the hardcoded, fleet-wide fixed set
# (object_catalog.fixed_catalog()): identical on every PC/user, edited only via
# _FIXED_CATALOG + an image rebuild. On an invalid catalog (a developer typo in
# the constant) every array is empty, success is false, and message carries the
# German reason.
---
string[]  type_names        # internal type key / block field value
string[]  labels_de         # German display label (parallel to type_names)
float64[] object_height_m   # object height (m); render + info
float64[] object_width_m    # footprint width (m); render box XY
string[]  color_hex         # render colour, e.g. "#f59e0b"
int32[]   max_instances     # len(tag_ids): copies the sim can detect / editor placement cap
bool      success
string    message           # German on failure
